<title>LEBANON: Beirut weekly T-bill issue raises 736 bln pounds.</title>
<headline>Beirut weekly T-bill issue raises 736 bln pounds.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lebanon's weekly treasury bill issue of September 19 raised 736 billion Lebanese pounds, the finance ministry said.</p>
<p>The previous issue raised 586 billion pounds.</p>
<p>The new issue posted a nominal surplus of subscription against maturity of 306 billion pounds. It raised the following amounts (in billions of pounds, previous week in brackets):</p>
<p>    Term			  Yield		    Amount</p>
<p>    Three months	    14.61 (14.61)	    87.4  (67.4)</p>
<p>    Six months		16.92 (16.92)	   135.9  (108.O)</p>
<p>    12 months		 17.80 (17.85)	    85.3  (118.2)</p>
<p>    24 months		 21.68 (21.74)	   427.4  (292.4)</p>
<p>The Lebanese pound closed at 1,558.75 to the U.S. dollar on Wednesday from 1,559.5 a week earlier.</p>
<p>- Beirut editorial (961 1) 864148 602056 645456</p>
